--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.6 IMPLEMENTATION OF RUNTIME WORKFLOW (END-TO-END)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

At runtime, the software behaves in this sequence:

1) User Authentication
- User signs in through UI.
- JWT token is issued by backend and used for protected API/WebSocket access.

2) Market Monitoring Loop
- Engine loop in `api.py` runs every configured interval.
- Prices + balances + statuses fetched for all exchanges.

3) Opportunity Analysis
- Pair routes generated.
- Spread and net-spread computed.
- Best route selected.

4) Decision Gating
- Threshold and cost-profitability checks.
- AI suggestion and risk breaker checks.
- Route inventory precheck before order placement.

5) Execution
- If all checks pass, execution handler triggers buy/sell sequence.
- Live or paper mode branch selected according to configuration.

6) Persistence and Broadcast
- Trade row persisted in DB.
- Feed/ledger events pushed via WebSocket to dashboard.
- UI updates immediately with status and settlement.

7) Learning and Adaptation
- LLM decision history keeps growing.
- Auto-retrain function can update GRU model from latest spreads.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.7 IMPLEMENTATION CHALLENGES AND PRACTICAL SOLUTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Challenge 1: Route appears profitable in UI but no execution
- Cause: gross spread > threshold, but net spread <= 0 after costs.
- Solution implemented: explicit net-spread guard and detailed feed messages.

Challenge 2: Exchange/API instability or temporary failures
- Solution implemented:
  - status flags per exchange
  - fallback data handling
  - cooldown and degraded-mode support

Challenge 3: Operator confusion over bot decisions
- Solution implemented:
  - execution feed messages (SUCCESS/FAILED/BLOCKED reasons)
  - execution ledger with status and settlement
  - separate chat vs feed panes in dashboard

Challenge 4: Continuous model relevance
- Solution implemented:
  - DB-driven retraining pipeline
  - model reload after successful retrain

